(7721929, 1270975, 114285, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Bear_Music:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m not sure I''d call this sort of mountain hiking a "trivial pursuit", actually, but based on what I''m seeing in the challenge a LOT of people think worthwhile, healthy, active things qualify as "trivial" :-) Anyway, it''s a lovely place/picture, Margaret. I wish I were well enough to do this :-( </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree - but these challenges always garner shoehorns, because a real trivial pursuit would bring about a boring photo IMHO. That''s why I try to avoid these challenges like the plague.